   "date": "2018-07-04T05:07:06Z",
   "subject": "Using nested SEPARABLE functions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Suppose I have a model with a random effect array, lnepsilon, with dim(n_s,n_t,n_l). The first dimension represents a Gaussian process and the other two represent AR1 processes.<br>Assuming an interaction between these processes, is it correct to define lnepsilon as: <br><div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">nll </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> GMRF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lnepsilon </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "vRElVCzNBAAJ",
   "from": "Kasper Kristensen",
   "author": "258b98968d0ad8b9",
   "date": "2018-07-05T09:41:30Z",
   "subject": "Re: Using nested SEPARABLE functions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">SEPARABLE(X,Y) works similar to Kronecker products in R. Y acts in the fastest running array dimension. So, your example is correct.</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><br>On Wednesday, July 4, 2018 at 7:07:06 AM UTC+2, Chris wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Suppose I have a model with a random effect array, lnepsilon, with dim(n_s,n_t,n_l). The first dimension represents a Gaussian process and the other two represent AR1 processes.<br>Assuming an interaction between these processes, is it correct to define lnepsilon as: <br><div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">nll </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> GMRF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lnepsilon </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span></div><div><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Rm-MUIkJBQAJ",
   "from": "Chris",
   "author": "59ce4b83b96c74fd",
   "date": "2018-07-06T04:07:40Z",
   "subject": "Re: Using nested SEPARABLE functions",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This all works fine. However, this same formulation does not work for simulation. For example, adding this into a SIMULATE block,<div><br><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  SIMULATE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> GMRF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))).</span><span style=\"color:#000\">simulate</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lnepsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  <br>    REPORT</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lnepsilon</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div>produces this error when calling obj$simulate():<br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">TMB has received an error </span><span style=\"color:#008\">from</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Eigen</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">The</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> following condition was </span><span style=\"color:#008\">not</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> met</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> tup</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&amp;&amp;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tup </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">).</span><span style=\"color:#000\">all</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Please</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> check your matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">vector bounds etc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">or</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> run your program through a </span><span style=\"color:#008\">debugger</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Breakpoint</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0x0000000021fed7a0</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> abort </span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#008\">from</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> space_size_tmb</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dll<br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#0  0x0000000021fed7a0 in abort ()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>   </span><span style=\"color:#008\">from</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> space_size_tmb</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dll<br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#1  0x00000000220f62bf in tmbutils::array&lt;double&gt;::index (this=this@entry=0x4419f40, tup=...)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    at C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/DOCUME~1/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">WIN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TMB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">include</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tmbutils</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">array</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">236</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#2  0x00000000220f5f83 in tmbutils::array&lt;double&gt;::perm (this=this@entry=0x441a000, p=...)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    at C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/DOCUME~1/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">WIN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TMB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">include</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tmbutils</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">array</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">256</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#3  0x00000000220f6455 in tmbutils::array&lt;double&gt;::rotate (this=this@entry=0x441a000, n=n@entry=1)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    at C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/DOCUME~1/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">WIN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TMB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">include</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tmbutils</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">array</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">282</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#4  0x00000000220d8f01 in density::SEPARABLE_t&lt;density::AR1_t&lt;density::N01&lt;double&gt; &gt;, density::SEPARABLE_t&lt;density::AR1_t&lt;density::N01&lt;double&gt; &gt;, density::GMRF_t&lt;double&gt; &gt; &gt;::sqrt_cov_scale (this=this@entry=0x441b850, u=...)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    at C</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#080\">/DOCUME~1/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">R</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">WIN</span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3.5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TMB</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">include</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tmbutils</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">density</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hpp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1202</span></div></code></div><div></div></div><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Does simulate() change how the output is stored (it doesn&#39;t seem to fit in the 3D array used previously)? or am I using it incorrectly?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Chris</div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div><br>On Thursday, 5 July 2018 21:41:30 UTC+12, Kasper Kristensen  wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">SEPARABLE(X,Y) works similar to Kronecker products in R. Y acts in the fastest running array dimension. So, your example is correct.<br><br><br>On Wednesday, July 4, 2018 at 7:07:06 AM UTC+2, Chris wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Suppose I have a model with a random effect array, lnepsilon, with dim(n_s,n_t,n_l). The first dimension represents a Gaussian process and the other two represent AR1 processes.<br>Assuming an interaction between these processes, is it correct to define lnepsilon as: <br><div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">nll </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_l</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> SEPARABLE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> AR1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rho_t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> GMRF</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">Q</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lnepsilon </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span></div><div><br></div></div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
